From 3e1d1a5bb156c1ef63c06e39fee422cda8f5d5ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hussain-maker <79055482+Hussain-maker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 18:50:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Add optional buff blacklist module
 (XPerlForever_AuraBlacklist)

Hides listed buffs on the target, focus, target-of-target and
focus-target frames. Each entry can be set to still show the buff when the
player cast it. Settings are on a new "Buff Blacklist" options tab: enable
toggle, add by spell ID or exact name, remove, "show if mine", and a merge
import from BetterBlizzFrames' aura blacklist (read-only). The list starts
empty and is stored account-wide in XPerlAuraBlacklistDB.

Midnight: a buff is only hidden when its spell ID is readable. While aura
data is restricted (arena, rated PvP, M+ and raid combat) X-Perl shows buffs
through Blizzard's AuraContainer; the module passes the list to it as
excludeSpellIDs (all IDs for friendly units, never-secret IDs otherwise).
"Show if mine" does not apply in that mode.

Core: two optional hooks, XPerl_BuffFilter in XPerl_Unit_UpdateBuffs and
XPerl_BuffContainerFilter in XPerl_AuraContainer_Create. Without the module
both are nil and behaviour is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
